# Server redirects for old addresses, read by Cloudflare when the site is deployed (Workers static
# assets: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/). The build copies this
# file to dist/_redirects; Cloudflare reads it and does not serve it as a page. Added 2026-11-14 in
# place of the in-page forwards, so a browser or a search engine gets a plain 301 (moved for good).
# Each address is listed with and without its closing slash, since a rule matches only what it says.
#
# A browser keeps the part of a link after "#" across a redirect, unless the new address has a
# "#" of its own, which then wins.

# The page for readers' critique was /disagree/ until 2026-09-25; the intro essay still links there.
/disagree/  /feedback/  301
/disagree   /feedback/  301

# /method/ became the first part of /about/ on 2026-10-21. No "#" here, so an old link to one part
# of the method (/method/#x) still lands on that part (/about/#x); the plain /method/ lands on the
# top of About, where the method is the first part.
/method/  /about/  301
/method   /about/  301

# /story/ became the second part of /about/ on 2026-10-21. The known links to it are to the plain
# address, so it goes straight to that part. A link to one story entry (/story/#x) lands at the
# start of the story part rather than on the entry.
/story/  /about/#story  301
/story   /about/#story  301
